{"nodes": [{"id": "technical_blueprint_v1_ports_and_adapters", "label": "Ports & Adapters (Hexagonal) Architecture", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "technical-blueprint-v1.md", "source_location": "\u00a70 Build philosophy, \u00a72.5", "rationale": "Three dependencies are gated outside the team's control (foreign payment/banking, procurement method, logistics+customs). Putting each behind an interface with a stub adapter lets the core and both surfaces be fully functional before any gate clears, and lets the real provider be swapped in with zero core rework. The gates decide WHICH adapter goes live, never WHETHER the system works.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "technical_blueprint_v1_modular_monolith", "label": "Modular Monolith (not microservices)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "technical-blueprint-v1.md", "source_location": "\u00a72.1", "rationale": "One deployable with strict internal module boundaries plus an in-process event bus gives DDD separation without distributed-systems overhead at MVP scale. Because modules already talk via events and interfaces, any module can later be extracted into a service without rewriting callers.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "technical_blueprint_v1_order_state_machine", "label": "Order State Machine & Transition Table", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "technical-blueprint-v1.md", "source_location": "\u00a71.4", "rationale": "Every transition is an event appended to an immutable order timeline so that tracking, audit and support all read from one source of truth rather than reconstructing history.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "technical_blueprint_v1_exception_matrix", "label": "Exception Matrix (ops policy)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "technical-blueprint-v1.md", "source_location": "\u00a71.5", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "technical_blueprint_v1_unified_tracking", "label": "Unified Multi-Leg Tracking Lifecycle", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "technical-blueprint-v1.md", "source_location": "\u00a71.6", "rationale": "Carrier, warehouse and marketplace statuses are heterogeneous and unreadable to customers; normalizing them into one legible lifecycle is what turns observable execution into trust, and never leaks raw carrier statuses.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "technical_blueprint_v1_money_value_object", "label": "Money Value Object", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "technical-blueprint-v1.md", "source_location": "\u00a72.2 RULE, \u00a72.4", "rationale": "Money is a typed value object {amount, currency}, DB-constrained and never produced by AI, because the ledger must be double-entry and deterministic; floats and implicit currency coercion are the classic source of unrecoverable financial error.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "technical_blueprint_v1_quote_engine", "label": "Quote / Landed-Cost Engine", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "technical-blueprint-v1.md", "source_location": "\u00a71.2, \u00a72.4", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "technical_blueprint_v1_revalidate_at_checkout", "label": "RULE: Revalidate at Checkout", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "technical-blueprint-v1.md", "source_location": "\u00a71.3", "rationale": "Offer, availability and FX all drift between quote and payment. Refreshing them immediately before the gateway and locking the quote for its TTL is the only way to keep the charged amount and the purchasable amount consistent; it is also the mitigation for AI extraction hallucination (R11).", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "technical_blueprint_v1_storeadapter_port", "label": "StoreAdapter Port", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "technical-blueprint-v1.md", "source_location": "\u00a72.5", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "technical_blueprint_v1_fxprovider_port", "label": "FxProvider Port", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "technical-blueprint-v1.md", "source_location": "\u00a72.5", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "technical_blueprint_v1_paymentgateway_port", "label": "PaymentGateway Port", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "technical-blueprint-v1.md", "source_location": "\u00a72.5", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "technical_blueprint_v1_procurementexecutor_port", "label": "ProcurementExecutor Port", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "technical-blueprint-v1.md", "source_location": "\u00a72.5", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "technical_blueprint_v1_carrieradapter_port", "label": "CarrierAdapter Port", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "technical-blueprint-v1.md", "source_location": "\u00a72.5", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "technical_blueprint_v1_customsestimator_port", "label": "CustomsEstimator Port", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "technical-blueprint-v1.md", "source_location": "\u00a72.5", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "technical_blueprint_v1_link_first_mvp", "label": "Link-First MVP Scope (no catalog/search)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "technical-blueprint-v1.md", "source_location": "\u00a71.2", "rationale": "A catalog would require merchandising, inventory and discovery surfaces that add no value when the customer already knows the product; one paste-a-link flow collapses the whole product surface to the single job to be done.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "technical_blueprint_v1_assisted_procurement", "label": "Assisted Procurement with AI Copilot", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "technical-blueprint-v1.md", "source_location": "\u00a71.2, \u00a72.5", "rationale": "The AI prepares all deterministic context and drives the cart to the pay button; a human confirms only the irreducible step (final purchase / 3DS challenge). Unsupervised browser automation is never the foundation, only an accelerant under a human gate.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "technical_blueprint_v1_manage_by_exception", "label": "RULE: Manage-by-Exception Ops Console", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "technical-blueprint-v1.md", "source_location": "\u00a71.5", "rationale": "Default view is the AI-ranked exception queue (margin-at-risk \u00d7 urgency), never a list of healthy orders \u2014 this is what lets a small operations team run high GMV.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "technical_blueprint_v1_double_entry_ledger", "label": "Double-Entry Deterministic Ledger", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "technical-blueprint-v1.md", "source_location": "\u00a72.2, \u00a72.4", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "technical_blueprint_v1_compliance_gate", "label": "Compliance Gate (master switch)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "technical-blueprint-v1.md", "source_location": "\u00a72.9", "rationale": "No architecture path may depend on concealment, account sharing, or bypassing marketplace/AML controls. AI cannot substitute for legal validation, so compliance stays the master switch before production regardless of technical readiness.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "technical_blueprint_v1_bounded_contexts", "label": "Bounded Contexts and Public Domain Events", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "technical-blueprint-v1.md", "source_location": "\u00a72.3", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "technical_blueprint_v1_async_workflows", "label": "Async Workers (FX refresh, procurement, tracking, recon)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "technical-blueprint-v1.md", "source_location": "\u00a72.7", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "technical_blueprint_v1_procurement_order_aggregate", "label": "ProcurementOrder as a Distinct Aggregate", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "technical-blueprint-v1.md", "source_location": "\u00a72.4 RULE", "rationale": "One customer order can split across several marketplaces, so Order and ProcurementOrder must be separate aggregates; every external marketplace order links back to its ProcurementOrder for audit, refunds and reconciliation.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "technical_blueprint_v1_sprint_sequence", "label": "Sprint Sequence S1\u2013S6 + Gate Swaps", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "technical-blueprint-v1.md", "source_location": "Part 3", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "technical_blueprint_v1_status_marker_taxonomy", "label": "DECISION / GATE / BUILD / RULE Status Markers", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "technical-blueprint-v1.md", "source_location": "Reading note", "rationale": "Markers are load-bearing rather than decorative: DECISION is a locked choice, GATE an external dependency to build interface-first, BUILD work to implement, RULE an enforced business rule. They make it explicit which statements may not be silently overridden.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "technical_blueprint_v1_ports_and_adapters", "target": "technical_blueprint_v1_modular_monolith", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "technical-blueprint-v1.md", "source_location": "\u00a70, \u00a72.1", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "technical_blueprint_v1_storeadapter_port", "target": "technical_blueprint_v1_ports_and_adapters", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "technical-blueprint-v1.md", "source_location": "\u00a72.5", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "technical_blueprint_v1_fxprovider_port", "target": "technical_blueprint_v1_ports_and_adapters", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "technical-blueprint-v1.md", "source_location": "\u00a72.5", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "technical_blueprint_v1_paymentgateway_port", "target": "technical_blueprint_v1_ports_and_adapters", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "technical-blueprint-v1.md", "source_location": "\u00a72.5", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "technical_blueprint_v1_procurementexecutor_port", "target": "technical_blueprint_v1_ports_and_adapters", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "technical-blueprint-v1.md", "source_location": "\u00a72.5", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "technical_blueprint_v1_carrieradapter_port", "target": "technical_blueprint_v1_ports_and_adapters", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "technical-blueprint-v1.md", "source_location": "\u00a72.5", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "technical_blueprint_v1_customsestimator_port", "target": "technical_blueprint_v1_ports_and_adapters", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "technical-blueprint-v1.md", "source_location": "\u00a72.5", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "technical_blueprint_v1_storeadapter_port", "target": "feasibility_revalidation_v0_2_universal_resolver", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "technical-blueprint-v1.md", "source_location": "\u00a72.5, Appendix", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "technical_blueprint_v1_assisted_procurement", "target": "feasibility_revalidation_v0_2_plan_follower_procurement", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "technical-blueprint-v1.md", "source_location": "Appendix mapping to v0.2", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "feasibility_revalidation_v0_2_deterministic_ledger_ai_matcher", "target": "technical_blueprint_v1_double_entry_ledger", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "technical-blueprint-v1.md", "source_location": "\u00a72.2 RULE", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "technical_blueprint_v1_manage_by_exception", "target": "feasibility_revalidation_v0_2_exception_classifier", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "technical-blueprint-v1.md", "source_location": "Appendix mapping to v0.2", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "technical_blueprint_v1_exception_matrix", "target": "technical_blueprint_v1_order_state_machine", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "technical-blueprint-v1.md", "source_location": "\u00a71.4\u20131.5", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "technical_blueprint_v1_unified_tracking", "target": "technical_blueprint_v1_carrieradapter_port", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "technical-blueprint-v1.md", "source_location": "\u00a71.6, \u00a72.5", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "technical_blueprint_v1_quote_engine", "target": "technical_blueprint_v1_money_value_object", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "technical-blueprint-v1.md", "source_location": "\u00a72.4", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "technical_blueprint_v1_carrieradapter_port", "target": "phase_0_3_logistics_feasibility_fulfillment_leg_model", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "technical-blueprint-v1.md", "source_location": "Appendix: v0.3 logistics \u2192 CarrierAdapter", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "technical_blueprint_v1_customsestimator_port", "target": "phase_0_3_logistics_feasibility_open_gates_0_4", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "technical-blueprint-v1.md", "source_location": "Appendix mapping to v0.3", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "feasibility_revalidation_v0_2_three_exogenous_gates", "target": "technical_blueprint_v1_ports_and_adapters", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "technical-blueprint-v1.md", "source_location": "\u00a70 \u2014 the gates are the stated reason for the port pattern", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "prototype_consumer_pwa_flow", "target": "technical_blueprint_v1_sprint_sequence", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "technical-blueprint-v1.md", "source_location": "Part 3 \u2014 prototype.html demonstrates the S2\u2013S4 surfaces", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "technical_blueprint_v1_procurement_order_aggregate", "target": "technical_blueprint_v1_order_state_machine", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "technical-blueprint-v1.md", "source_location": "\u00a72.4", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "technical_blueprint_v1_async_workflows", "target": "technical_blueprint_v1_fxprovider_port", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "technical-blueprint-v1.md", "source_location": "\u00a72.7 FX refresh worker", "weight": 1.0}], "hyperedges": [{"id": "gated_seam_ports", "label": "The Six Gated Seam Ports", "nodes": ["technic